# CRTPlayer 2.0 for Miyoo Mini Plus (OnionOS)

A drop-in companion app for the OnionOS FFplay video player that turns your
video playback into a real CRT experience — scanlines, glow, grain, a
choice of physical TV bezels, and a live in-app filter menu — all
switchable on the fly with a button press, no need to leave the app or
touch a script.

## What's new in 2.0

* **Live filter toggle** — turn the whole CRT effect on/off instantly
while a video is playing
* **Three tuned presets**, each with its own on-screen label:

  * **Warm Glow** — clean scanlines, punchy color, soft highlight lift
  * **Classic CRT** — the reference "textbook" CRT look
  * **VHS Tape** — heavier grain and scanlines, warm tint, worn-tape mood
* **A custom filter menu** — pause, pick exactly which effects you want
(scanlines, saturation, vignette, glow, grain, tint) in any
combination, and resume with your own custom look
* **Five bezel options** — four physical/illustrated TV frames, cyclable
live, plus a "no bezel" full-screen mode
* All of the above work together — pick any preset or custom combo with
any bezel, at any time, without restarting the app

## What it does

* Scanlines (tuned to avoid color fringing on chroma-subsampled video)
* Color/saturation boost
* Vignette (darkened corners)
* Film grain
* Warm color tint
* Highlight glow
* Real TV bezel frames around your video, cycled live
* A pause menu for fully custom filter combinations

All done via ffplay's built-in `-vf` filtergraph and a background
button-listener script — no source modification, no recompiling.

## Requirements

* Miyoo Mini Plus running OnionOS
* The standard **FFplay / Video Player** app already installed (this mod
uses the same shared system ffplay binary — it does not bundle its own)
* Credit to [Steward-fu](https://steward-fu.github.io/website/handheld/miyoo-mini/parasyte_build_ffplay.htm)
and [bobotrax](https://github.com/bobotrax/ffplay_Miyoo) for the
original FFplay port this builds on

## Installation

1. Download this zip and extract its contents into a new folder named
`CRTPlayer`.
2. Copy that `CRTPlayer` folder into `/App/` at the root of your SD card,
so you end up with `/App/CRTPlayer/` containing `launch.sh`,
`config.json`, `icon.png`, and all the bezel/label PNGs directly (not
nested another level deep).
3. Restart the device.
4. You should see a new **CRTPlayer** icon in your Apps menu, alongside
the regular Video Player.
5. Videos are read from the same `Media/Videos` folder as the normal
player — no need to duplicate your files.

## Controls

|Button|Action|
|-|-|
|**L**|Turn the CRT filter fully on/off|
|**R**|Cycle presets: Warm Glow → Classic CRT → VHS Tape|
|**R2**|Cycle bezels: Bezel 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → No Bezel|
|**L2**|Open/close the custom filter menu|
|**Up / Down** (in menu)|Move the cursor between filters|
|**R** (in menu)|Toggle the highlighted filter on/off|

Closing the custom menu switches you to a **Custom** look built from
whichever filters you checked — it works alongside the three presets and
any bezel, and stays selected until you pick a preset with R or open the
menu again.

## Known limitations

* Position tracking on toggle is approximate (based on elapsed time, not
ffplay's true internal position) — switching modes right after a manual
seek may land you a little off from where you actually were. Normal
playback and toggling is accurate to within a second or so.
* The custom menu pauses the video while open; there's a brief
(roughly 1 second or less) interruption each time you toggle a filter,
switch presets, or switch bezels, since each change restarts playback
under the hood.
* This is a stripped ffplay build — several common ffmpeg filters aren't
available (`eq`, `rgbashift`, `tmix`, `drawtext` all fail to launch).
Everything in this release only uses filters confirmed working on this
exact build.

## The filter chain (for tinkerers)

Base preset filters (before bezel compositing):

```sh
# Warm Glow
hflip,vflip,drawgrid=w=iw:h=4:t=1:c=black@0.2,hue=s=1.4,vignette,lutyuv=y='val\*1.1+8',noise=alls=7:allf=t

# Classic CRT
hflip,vflip,drawgrid=w=iw:h=3:t=1:c=black@0.2,hue=s=1.3,vignette,noise=alls=8:allf=t,colorbalance=rs=0.05:gs=0.04:bs=-0.05

# VHS Tape
hflip,vflip,drawgrid=w=iw:h=3:t=1:c=black@0.45,hue=s=1.05,vignette,noise=alls=15:allf=t,colorbalance=rs=0.15:gs=0.05:bs=-0.15,lutyuv=y='val\*1.1+8'
```

Custom menu filters map to these individual segments — mix and match any
combination:

|Filter|Segment|
|-|-|
|Scanlines|`drawgrid=w=iw:h=4:t=1:c=black@0.2`|
|Saturation|`hue=s=1.4`|
|Vignette|`vignette`|
|Glow|`lutyuv=y='val\*1.1+8'`|
|Grain|`noise=alls=7:allf=t`|
|Tint|`colorbalance=rs=0.05:gs=0.04:bs=-0.05`|

Bezels composite in via `movie=`+`overlay`, each with its own measured
scale/position since every bezel photo/illustration has a differently
sized screen cutout — see `launch.sh` for the exact values per bezel.

## Credits

Built and tuned by Jack\_Appleseed. Built on the OnionOS FFplay
port originally by Steward-fu, packaged for OnionOS by bobotrax and the
OnionUI team.

## Support

I love digging into old hardware and finding ways to make it do things
it was never designed for — there's something genuinely satisfying about
poking through a stripped-down embedded system, hitting dead ends, and
eventually getting a device to do something new. CRTPlayer
started as a "wouldn't it be cool if" idea and turned into a real deep
dive into shell scripting, filter chains, and reverse-engineering
hardware I don't have full documentation for. I build and share mods
like this because I like making things other people can enjoy, not
because I expect anything back — but I'm currently between jobs, so if
you got some use or nostalgia out of this project, any support genuinely
helps and is deeply appreciated.

If you'd like to support the project, you can buy me a coffee here:
